    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d26">

                <pb facs="0080" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v06/pg48"/>

                <head>26. Telegram From the Embassy in Cuba to the Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d26-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-03-03T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 3, 1958—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>498. If steps planned in Deptel 462<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d26-f2"/> should become public knowledge, situation in Cuba
                    now such that result might be downfall Batista before elections.</p>
                <p>Prior to taking formal steps outlined in Deptel 462 recommend Department consider authorizing me inform
                        Batista such steps will be taken
                    unless he agrees to take immediately part or all actions outlined in Embtel 490.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d26-f3"/></p>
                <p>It has been our hope that such actions (Embtel
                    490) will lead Cuban people to believe that solution of present situation can be
                    obtained peacefully through elections rather than by violence.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
